Fix $l,n$. Fix $p$ so that $n-p=2k$ for some $k\geq 0$, and $r \in \{0, 1, ..., min(p,l+2)\}$. 
Let $\cc_\l$ be any element of $\Q\Sym_{r}$ such that the 
$\C\Sym_r$ Specht module $\SS_\l \cong \C\Sym_{r} \cc_\l$
(here $\Sym_0$ is the trivial group). 
Then $\cc_\l \otimes 1_{p-r} \in \Q\Sym_p$ and can be regarded as an element of $J_l(p,p)$ by the obvious inclusion, 
\ppmm{provided that $\Q\subset\K$}. 



As in \cite{KadarYu}  
\[
\Deltaa^{n}_{(p,\lambda)} \;\; \cong  \;\; J_l(n,p) ( \cc_\l \otimes 1_{p-r}) / J_l^{p-2}(n,p)
\]
where $(p,\lambda) \in\Lambda_{l,n}$ as per \ref{eq:simples}; 
$J_l^{p-2}(p,n)$ is as per \ref{de:Jln}.


It will now be convenient to fix $ \Deltaa^{n}_{(p,\lambda)}$  precisely by choosing $\cc_\l$.

