Obviously there is a map $(4,(2))\rightarrow (2,(1^2))$, so dim-hom $\geq 1$ on the right unless the $(4,(1^2))$ is glued under - but this would imply a map that we 
noted above  
is not there. Thus dim-hom on the left is nonzero. This forces 
